      "id": "KFB-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "A diagonal doubled kernel controls each target slice",
      "anchor": "lifts-kernel-slice",
      "statement": "For the Fock polynomial of a chain step a target slice is square-integrable, and its squared norm is bounded by a constant times a power of the source quotient height.",
      "hypotheses": "Use the Weil pair, the Fock vector, the rank and Witt condition, the Siegel–Weil integrability and Eisenstein value for its self-pair, the regularity estimate, the height bound for the doubled embedding, and the specified Haar measures.",
