      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Doubling Φ with itself identifies its absolute square on the diagonal with the norm of the doubled kernel. The target mean is a regular Eisenstein value; pulling its height estimate back to the diagonal and restoring the volume bounds the squared slice norm.",
