    {
      "id": "KFB-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "The absolute triple-integral bound permits the seesaw exchange",
      "anchor": "lifts-kernel-swap",
      "statement": "Let Nᵢ dominate the target L² norm of each source slice and let ∫Nᵢ|uᵢ|=Mᵢ<∞. The integral of |K₁u₁ K₂u₂| over the two source copies and the target is at most M₁M₂. With pointwise integrability of each lift, the lifts are in L² and their pairing equals the double source integral of the kernel pairing times u₁ conjugate(u₂).",
      "hypotheses": "Jointly measurable kernels and σ-finite measure spaces. In the arithmetic application the source has finite volume, the cusp inputs are rapidly decreasing, kernels have moderate growth at each fixed target and their squared target norms have moderate growth. The arithmetic action gives descent to the quotients.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-kernel-majorant",
        "lifts-kernel-pair"
      ],
