  "outstanding": [
    "The quotient-height estimate uses finite volume and rapid decay. The regularity and polynomial growth of the Eisenstein family and the growth estimate under the doubled embedding are separate inputs. The nonnegative-integral argument controls the interchange of quotient integrations here."
  ]
